  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "MSRVs 2-PCV-001-0023, 2-PCV-001-0031, 2-PCV-001-0041, and 2-PCV-001-0179 failed above their setpoints due to corrosion bonding to the valve seat. As a result of corrosion bonding, the force required to break the crystal structure of the corrosion bond alters the mechanical setpoint of the pilot valve...commonly known to the industry as setpoint drift. Simmering valves result in mechanical setpoint drift and is generally the result of low stellite in the seat.",
    "cause_code": "TBD",
    "category": "provisional",
    "theme": "MSRV pilot valve corrosion bonding / setpoint drift",
    "provisional": true
  },
